'''Teacher Cybear''' (メタックマ, ''Metakkuma'', '''Metabear''') is a [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] variant of [[Teacher Bear]] that appears in [[Special Events|Event Stages]]. He was added in [[Version 8.0 Update|Version 8.0]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Teacher Cybear
|image = E 057.png
|appearance = [[Forged to Kill (Deadly)]]<br>
[[Hard Restart Lv.7]]
|money drop = 550¢ - 2,172¢
}}

==Enemy==
Teacher Cybear has 600 range with extremely fast, single-target attacks that do 999,999 damage, though he only has a measly 50 health and just 3 speed to go with.

==Strategy==
Because of his lethal damage, low health, Metal trait and attack type, the most effective way to take him down is to spam cheap meatshields. Bring units like [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]], [[Li'l Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Cat]], [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cat]], [[Pumpcat (Rare Cat)|Pumpcat]], [[Awa-Odori Cat (Rare Cat)|Awa-Odori Cat]], [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Boogie Cat]], [[Coin Cat (Special Cat)|Coin Cat]], or [[Catburger (Special Cat)|Catburger]]. You could also use Li'l Mohawk Cat's crit [[Talents|Talent]] to save some time. The [[Battle Items#Cat CPU|Cat CPU]] can help with spamming the units as quick as possible.

Otherwise, [[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Macho]] can be used to sponge up to 12 hits from Cybear, slightly speeding up the fight. [[Kyubey Cat (Rare Cat)|Kyubey Cat]] also works well due to its low cost and 40% chance to [[Survive]] a lethal strike. [[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]] could work better as it will always survive, but its high cost (240¢, while most other meatshields are around 75~150¢) often puts it out of the question.

In [[Hard Restart Lv.7]], Teacher Cybear appears with peons, which can be used as stepping stones for Critical [[Wave Attack|Wave]]/[[Surge Attack|Surge Attackers]] like [[Valentine's Neneko (Super Rare Cat)|Valentine's Neneko]], [[Backhoe Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Neo Backhoe Cat]] and [[Kubiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|E. Kubilan Pasalan]].

