==Trivia==
*This enemy has some interesting history, as he was one of the few enemies (the others are [[Metal Cyclone]], [[CyberFace]] and [[Professor A.]]) to actually be unimplemented for a certain amount of time. After years of rotting away in the game data, Teacher Cybear finally got his due in the [[Version 8.0 Update]].
**Before he was implemented, Teacher Cybear was a [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemy with 1,000 HP, 80 damage, 150 range, 15 speed, no abilities, no wave-like effect in his attack animation, and a money drop of 55,000¢ (basically an exact copy of [[Gory]], but with a much higher money drop).
*Although the pronouns in [[Teacher Bear]]'s description were changed to they/them in [[Version 14.7 Update|Version 14.7]], Teacher Cybear's description was not updated accordingly, meaning Cybear's still refers to Teacher Bear as he/him.
*His Japanese description mentions that he was freeloading at [[The Face]]'s house for 6 years, which is the length of time between the release of [[Nyanko Daisensou]] and the release of update 8.0.
**His Japanese description also implies that Teacher Cybear is wearing an animatronic mascot costume of himself, almost like a Matyroshka doll.
*In the Japanese version, Teacher Cybear is a reference to the [[wikipedia:San-X|San-X]] character [[wikipedia:Rilakkuma|Rilakkuma]]. He has a similar name (Metakkuma), is described as a mascot costume, and lived rent-free with The Face (named Kaoru-kun in Japanese), referencing how the original Rilakkuma 4koma had the character relaxing in the apartment of an office worker named Kaoru. Additionally, Rilakkuma has a zipper on his back, but who or what is inside the costume is unknown; by contrast, Teacher Cybear's Japanese description states exactly what's in the costume.
**Based on his color scheme, Teacher Cybear might also represent the white-furred [[wikia:rilakkuma:Korilakkuma|Korilakkuma]], whose button suggests that, like Rilakkuma, it isn't an actual bear.
*The phrase 重い腰を上げて ''omoi koshi o agete'' in his Japanese description means "to bestir oneself; to make an effort after being inactive/unmotivated", but literally translates to "to lift one's heavy waist". It's likely meant both ways here, with Cybear both being unproductive when he was freeloading at The Face's house and weighing a ton because of his Metal trait.
*He has the highest DPS of any character.
*He is tied with the [[Dummy (Enemy Base)|Dummy]] for the third-highest attack power of any character, the second being [[Filibuster Obstructa]], who does 1,000,000 damage, and the first being [[Metafilibuster (Enemy)|Metafilibuster]], who does 3,000,000 damage.
*Prior to the [[Version 11.0 Update]], Teacher Cybear had 800 range instead of 600, and waited 0 frames between attacks instead of 3.

